About the job

We’re looking for a hands-on engineer who combines strong development skills with product thinking, quality assurance, and delivery ownership.
📍Kathmandu, Nepal | Full-time🏢 Anchor Points
Working under our Technical Lead, you’ll build and improve applications while helping ensure features are complete, intuitive, reliable, and ready for customers. You should be comfortable writing code, clarifying requirements, organizing sprint tasks, and identifying gaps in functionality and user experience.
Your responsibilities
Develop and maintain full-stack features, APIs, and integrations.
Translate business requirements into clear Jira tickets, user stories, and acceptance criteria.
Take ownership of assigned features from requirements through development, testing, and release.
Identify workflow gaps, edge cases, usability issues, and opportunities for improvement.
Review product quality, including functionality, interface consistency, wording, and presentation.
Collaborate with developers and QA to investigate issues, verify fixes, and prevent regressions.
Support sprint planning, backlog refinement, and coordination of blockers and dependencies.
Build AI-powered features and use AI development tools with careful review and validation.
Communicate progress, risks, and proposed solutions clearly.

What we’re looking for
Approximately 4–6+ years of software development experience.
Strong full-stack development skills, with backend experience in PHP/Laravel or Python and frontend experience with JavaScript frameworks.
Experience with REST APIs, databases, Git, and collaborative development.
Strong understanding of testing, acceptance criteria, and release readiness.
Experience using Jira or similar tools to organize development work.
Practical experience with AI-assisted development; AI integration experience is a plus.
A strong eye for usability, quality, and customer-facing presentation.
Clear communication, sound judgment, and proactive follow-through.

Experience with SaaS applications, automated testing, and ownership of features across the complete development lifecycle would be valuable.
This is a hands-on development role. We’re looking for someone who contributes code regularly while taking responsibility for how the product works and feels to its users.




